  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given $P(A)=\\frac{3}{8},$ $P(B)=\\frac{1}{3},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{17}{24},$ determine whether $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events.",
  "worked_solution": "To check if $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive, we must check that $P(A\\cap B)=0.$\n\nWe can calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{17}{24} & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{3}-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{17}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+8-17}{24} \\\\  & =0\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ and $B$ are mutually exclusive events.",
